comments[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-09T10:23:30.869Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: all-status coverage combined verdict search found completed pm-2qqcgl, which correctly made exact coverage fail closed, but no owner for the Vitest threshold/runner attribution mismatch. Full predecessor data/history and live open/in-progress lists read before creation. Source evidence is scripts/run-tests.mjs runValidation; local focused receipt has 199/199 assertions passing and runner exit3. Follow-up remains open/unclaimed."
  "2026-11-10T05:50:58.224Z","harness:codex","The exact production-preparation run42759813393 now reproduces this issue at full scale:925 files and12365 assertions passed with0 assertion failures; one SDK telemetry guard branch was uncovered; Vitest and the exact gate both returned nonzero and the runner falsely said test execution failed. Use a fresh invocation-owned JSON assertion report while retaining both independent process/gate exit codes so reporter errors and interruptions cannot be relabeled as successful execution. No percentage threshold, denominator or admission gate is relaxed."
  "2026-11-10T06:21:55.107Z","harness:codex","Reproduced the release escape in Auto Release 42759813393 on merged main baf182d: 925 files and 12365 assertions passed, but exact coverage refused one statement and branch in alias pruning. Before the fix, two isolated real-process fixtures both failed their intended diagnostic assertion while preserving exit 3 and a real 50 percent branch shortfall. The runner now reads a fresh invocation-owned structured receipt from the public Vitest lifecycle, independently names assertion results, process exit, and exact coverage, and leaves malformed, missing, interrupted and zero-test evidence non-passing. Explicit reporters retain both MCP enforcement and receipt collection; inherited receipt paths are removed before builds and nested runs. Reporter types use the supported vitest/node entrypoint, with narrowed file-level MCP log attribution. No coverage exclusions, threshold reductions, SDK hooks, or release bypasses were added."
  "2026-11-10T06:48:49.614Z","harness:codex","Linked verification: the four-file runner/reporter/process cohort passed 70 assertions, and pm-01kwb2 passed all 31 telemetry cases. The first complete local monolithic run retained one real failure: the packed continuation fixture could not resolve npm/package.json under the host Node 26 global-module layout. Vitest emitted no coverage summary, and the new diagnostic correctly reported Tests failed, Vitest exit 1, and exact-gate failure with exit 3. Preserve this failed attempt. Verified the installed npm manifest through NODE_PATH=<installed-npm-root>; the unchanged packed-continuation fixture plus all 58 runner cases then passed. Repeat the linked full coverage command with that process-local module path; no source or quality-policy exception is involved."
  "2026-11-10T07:12:22.065Z","harness:codex","Complete monolithic linked coverage now passes, run test-local-mwacqaot-tcbrad: all 70204 lines, 74671 statements, 15552 functions and 57904 branches covered across 843 source files, zero integer deficits. The original full source selectors, exact thresholds, MCP contract gate and process exit codes remain unchanged. The corrected environment was confined to this local invocation. Project type checks, explicit current-Vitest reporter type checks, complete static quality and bounded mutation assurance all passed; the earlier failed environment attempt remains visible. The runner unit assertion also uses the native path join for Windows portability."
  "2026-11-10T07:17:52.197Z","harness:codex","Final verification: 926 test files and 12383 assertions passed, with one pre-existing skipped file and three skipped assertions. The base artifact passes at 19994139 distribution bytes against the unchanged 20000000-byte cap and 23402553 runtime-bundle bytes against 25000000. Latest pm-changelog 2026.11.7 generated and checked the complete changelog. Final security scan caught a local module-root path in one evidence comment; a literal-scoped dry run confirmed one history replacement, and the audited redaction preserved zero hash mismatches and all recorded outcomes. The scan now passes."
  "2026-11-10T07:25:13.626Z","harness:codex","Final delivery inventory: all 3256 items are readable with no omission receipt; zero items are in progress. Both follow-up owners are closed and unclaimed with structured closure evidence. Packaged npx and bunx smoke passed for nine packages. Tracker validation verifies all 3256 histories with zero drift or chain/hash mismatches; its separate warn-only resolution-field check retains 170 warnings in other existing items. No warning or original failed test attempt was erased. Package activation metadata reflects the required package-owned changelog installation."
  "2026-11-10T07:37:39.763Z","harness:codex","PR #1698 head f2b275c required static job 129692766121 failed its post-close defect-evidence ratchet: exactly missing_escape_class and missing_gate_evidence on this item; boundary and recurrence-policy checks passed. The initial local static run preceded closure, so it did not exercise terminal-item admission. Added review_caught_late classification for a pre-publication validation diagnosis and gate_strengthened evidence naming the real-process deliberate-coverage-refusal fixture, full canonical coverage and hosted static/coverage checks. No gate policy or source selector is relaxed. GitHub report https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1697 is mapped to canonical pm-01kwb2 plus this related diagnostic owner; no duplicate item is needed."
  "2026-11-10T08:08:10.361Z","harness:codex","Post-close validation is now complete at the static-stage boundaries: the typed defect-evidence gate passes, the Node 24 full run passed SDK entrypoint and CLI transport budgets, and its graph-composition ratchet correctly identified two prose-only references added by the new prospective-closure note. Added the actual related edges to the existing context owner; graph composition returns to the unchanged 1233-gap ceiling. The remaining record-integrity and bounded mutation stages pass (345 killed, 7 reviewed equivalent, 352 total). Secret scanning passes. Preserve the earlier qualified Node 26 authoring-budget failure under related pm-bj7rq0; separate Node 24 and Node 26 import comparisons passed without code or budget changes. Implementation bytes are unchanged from the fully reviewed f2b275c head, with 12383 passing monolithic assertions and exact complete coverage."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-10T07:12:25.856Z","harness:codex","A Vitest nonzero exit can represent assertion, reporter or coverage refusal. Preserve process and exact-gate failures, but attribute assertion results only from a fresh structured lifecycle receipt. A linked test --add registers commands; execute them explicitly with --run and verify the recorded result."
  "2026-11-10T07:52:55.080Z","harness:codex","Run terminal-defect assurance after structured fields are populated and closure is represented: a pre-close static pass does not certify a later terminal record. Existing typed escape classification and gate_evidence are distinct from narrative comments and test links. Preserve separate failed benchmark attempts and supported-runtime comparisons; do not relabel a qualified budget refusal as an unqualified runner."
